  "row3": {
   "x": 0,
   "y": 1770,
   "text": "Settings and import",
   "kind": "title1",
   "maxW": 2872
  },
  "flow": {
   "x": 2952,
   "y": 0,
   "w": 360,
   "text": "Tap through: Sign in → trip list. Gear → Settings. ⋮ → Sign out. A card → its trip (Edinburgh is a trip shared with you; Liverpool is your own). Back arrows return; system back does the same. Dialogs close via X.",
   "kind": null,
   "fill": "blue"
  },
  "idioms": {
   "x": 2952,
   "y": 420,
   "w": 360,
   "text": "Idioms: one scrolling list with Now / Upcoming / Past headers (empty groups hide, so no tabs). A navigation bar with four destinations, Trips, Calendar, Reports and Profile, since the web app grew the last three; Settings stays behind the gear, Sign out in the overflow menu. Booking form is a full-screen dialog. Row ⋮ opens a bottom sheet. Delete trip is a dialog. Pill buttons and an extended FAB “Add a booking”.",
   "kind": null,
   "fill": "gray"
  },
  "states": {
   "x": 2952,
   "y": 1035,
   "w": 360,
   "text": "Round two boards the states: offline banner (amber, same words as the web app) and the offline page the service worker serves; a loading trip with its skeleton; the not-found text; a trip whose deletion was interrupted (amber callout, no booking actions); Rename as a text-field dialog with its one error, “Give the trip a name”.",
   "kind": null,
   "fill": "gray"
  },
  "gaps": {
   "x": 2952,
   "y": 1455,
   "w": 360,
   "text": "Shown as the product is, not fixed: no way to add a trip (trips come from imports and merges); booking Delete, Merge, Disconnect and Sign out have no confirmation; rows say \"Car\", the form says \"Car rental\"; \"Import anyway\" reports a raw outcome token; sign-in errors show raw Firebase text; a sharee never sees who owns the trip.",
   "kind": null,
   "fill": "orange"
  },
  "theme": {
   "x": 2952,
   "y": 2070,
   "w": 360,
   "text": "Theme: Material 3 roles from the web app's zinc palette; primary zinc-900 (zinc-100 in dark), amber tertiary for warnings, red error. Geist with system fallback. Pill buttons and FAB, 12px cards, 28px sheets and dialogs. Launcher icon is adaptive: dark square background, white paper plane foreground.",
   "kind": null,
   "fill": "gray"
  },
  "row4": {
   "x": 0,
   "y": 2805,
   "text": "States and edge cases",
   "kind": "title1",
   "maxW": 2872
  },
  "row5": {
   "x": 0,
   "y": 3840,
   "text": "Reports, profile and reminders",
   "kind": "title1",
   "maxW": 2872
  },
  "row6": {
   "x": 0,
   "y": 4875,
   "text": "Dark set",
   "kind": "title1",
   "maxW": 2872
  },
  "features": {
   "x": 2952,
   "y": 3840,
   "w": 360,
   "fill": "blue",
   "text": "Reports, Profile and reminders mirror the web app as built: days per country and trips per year, a map of countries and airports (a sketch here), the travel profile with documents folded and loyalty open, passport and visa reminders in red (before the trip ends) or amber (within six months after), and Settings’ import sections: TripIt preview with reasons grouped, calendar files and feeds, Google Calendar, the calendar link."
  },
  "dark": {
   "x": 2952,
   "y": 4875,
   "w": 360,
   "fill": "gray",
   "text": "Dark set: the same theme tokens as 14, on a trip page, the booking form with address suggestions (the Where field offers places from three typed characters; Add waits while a pick’s details load), Settings and Reports."
  },
  "row7": {
   "x": 0,
   "y": 5910,
   "text": "Calendar and at a glance",
   "kind": "title1",
   "maxW": 2872
  },
  "round3": {
   "x": 2952,
   "y": 5910,
   "w": 360,
   "fill": "blue",
   "text": "Round three: the calendar (a month of weeks, Monday first, each trip a bar across its days, shared trips violet, a carried-over bar starts with an ellipsis, today ringed) as a fourth destination in the navigation bar; Profile leads with a table of each loyalty program’s account, balance and status, the full entries folded below; a booking shows the viewer’s program its provider belongs to under the provider line; the Reports map gains smaller dots for stays and other places whose booking knows its spot."
  }
 },
